      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1531307987809144832",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Check out the post, and other memos I've sent to the @scale_AI team, below!\n\nhttps://t.co/7AlBgxCnK6",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1531307989461635072"
    },
    {
      "attachments": {
        "media_keys": [
          "3_1531307164014235649"
        ]
      },
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2022-05-30T16:14:09.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1531307987809144832"
      ],
      "id": "1531307987809144832",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 2,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 52,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 2,
        "retweet_count": 2
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1531307986412482561",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "The opposite is also unfortunately true—pessimistic people get less done.\n\nThey will estimate that things will take much longer than they should, and in the process, they WILL take longer than they should.\n\nAdded up over any meaningful period of time, it's crippling. https://t.co/xhNSdDN8py",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1531307987809144832"
    },
    {
      "attachments": {
        "media_keys": [
          "3_1531306669841403904"
        ]
      },
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2022-05-30T16:14:08.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1531307986412482561"
      ],
      "id": "1531307986412482561",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 8,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 43,
        "quote_count": 2,
        "reply_count": 3,
        "retweet_count": 8
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1531307984017428480",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "You can see this in a histogram of all marathon times.\n\nPeople are really good at accomplishing their goals—lots of people get marathon timings right below 3, 3.5, 4 hrs, etc\n\nHumans are motivated by goals, and these goals are influenced by our intrinsic optimism of our potential https://t.co/zOatgy1Nu7",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1531307986412482561"
    },
    {
      "attachments": {
        "media_keys": [
          "3_1531306218643333121"
        ]
      },
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2022-05-30T16:14:08.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1531307984017428480"
      ],
      "id": "1531307984017428480",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 2,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 41,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 2,
        "retweet_count": 6
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1531307982473994240",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "The scope, or how long we say something will take, influences how long something takes.\n\nWhen we say things will take a long time, they will take a long time.\n\nWhen we say things will take a short amount of time, they will take less time. https://t.co/QI7DIz0zgp",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1531307984017428480"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2022-05-30T16:14:08.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1531307982473994240"
      ],
      "id": "1531307982473994240",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 268,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 543,
        "quote_count": 25,
        "reply_count": 28,
        "retweet_count": 101
      },
      "text": "Posting a memo I sent to the @scale_AI team back in 2019.\n\nThe core idea is that most organizations fall prey to a slow death of optimism, causing a slow, excruciating halt.\n\nThread below 👇\n\nhttps://t.co/7AlBgxCnK6",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1531307982473994240"
    },
    {
      "attachments": {
        "media_keys": [
          "3_1530305732263833600",
          "3_1530305732268003329"
        ]
      },
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2022-05-27T21:51:33.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1530305735040458752"
      ],
      "id": "1530305735040458752",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 2,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 110,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 4
      },
      "text": "Lily Yang, a @scale_AI intern, drew a WATERCOLOR painting of her team from her internship 🎨\n\nIronically, this is our Mapping team, where maps are generally NOT up for artistic interpretation.\n\nAnd to be absolutely clear, no DALL-E was involved in the making of this masterpiece🥹 https://t.co/c1dvQOzUyt",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1530305735040458752"
    },
    {
      "attachments": {
        "media_keys": [
          "3_1529517834573070336"
        ]
      },
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "created_at": "2022-05-25T17:40:59.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1529517900968624129"
      ],
      "id": "1529517900968624129",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 8,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 144,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 4,
        "retweet_count": 14
      },
      "text": "I had the opportunity to visit @Walmart Home Office, and found this amazing sign in the hallway.\n\nRelentless customer centricity is inspiring and energizing!\n\nOne of our credos at @scale_ai is “Customer comes first.”—that being said I think Walmart says it better! https://t.co/rVsnnIWt5k",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1529517900968624129"
    },
